["Below is a simple example of how you might implement such a system in C using POSIX Threads for thread safety and mutexes to avoid concurrent access from different threads. For simplicity, let's consider only two logging levels - info and error. Moreover, remote logging services integration and buffer management are not implemented due to their complexity. Also, note that this is a simplified version of the problem and does not cover all potential requirements and edge cases for a production-level system.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <pthread.h>

// Define logging severity levels
typedef enum {
    LOG_LEVEL_INFO,
    LOG_LEVEL_ERROR
} LogLevel;

typedef struct {
    char *message;
    LogLevel level;
} LogEntry;

typedef struct {
    pthread_mutex_t mutex;
    LogEntry **entries;
    int size;
} Logger;

void initLogger(Logger *logger) {
    pthread_mutex_init(&logger->mutex, NULL);
    logger->size = 0;
    logger->entries = NULL;
}

// Add a new log entry to the logger (Synchronous)
void addLogSync(Logger *logger, LogLevel level, char *message) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&logger->mutex);

    // Allocate memory for new entry
    LogEntry *newEntry = malloc(sizeof(LogEntry));
    newEntry->level = level;
    newEntry->message = strdup(message); 

    logger->entries = realloc(logger->entries, sizeof(LogEntry*) * (logger->size + 1));
    logger->entries[logger->size] = newEntry;
    logger->size++;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&logger->mutex);
}

// Add a new log entry to the logger (Asynchronous)
void *addLogAsync(void *arg) {
    Logger *logger = ((void **)arg)[0];
    LogLevel level = ((int*)arg)[1];
    char *message = ((char **)arg)[2];

    addLogSync(logger, level, message);
    return NULL;
}

// Destroy the logger and free all resources
void destroyLogger(Logger *logger) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&logger->mutex);

    for (int i = 0; i < logger->size; i++) {
        free(logger->entries[i]->message);
        free(logger->entries[i]);
    }
    free(logger->entries);

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&logger->mutex);
    pthread_mutex_destroy(&logger->mutex);
}
```
In a real world scenario, the logger would likely be extended to include functions for remote logging services integration and efficient buffer management. Moreover, handling different severity levels and integrating new logging protocols will require additional design decisions that are beyond this simple example's scope. This code should serve as a foundation upon which to build more advanced functionality.
"]

