['Here is the Java method as per your specifications:

```java
import java.nio.*;
import java.net.*;
import java.security.*;
import javax.xml.bind.DatatypeConverter;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;
import java.io.IOException;

public class RemoteAddressHash {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(RemoteAddressHash.class.getName());
    private static final int MAX_RECONNECTION_ATTEMPTS = 3;

    public String getRemoteAddressMD5Async(String remoteAddr) throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        AsynchronousSocketChannel channel = null;

        try {
            InetSocketAddress address = new InetSocketAddress(InetAddress.getByName(remoteAddr), 80); // assuming port is 80 for the example
            int reconnectionAttempts = 0;

            do {
                channel = AsynchronousSocketChannel.open();

                if (channel.isOpen()) {
                    Future<Void> connectionFuture = channel.connect(address);

                    try {
                        connectionFuture.get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS); // setting a timeout of 5 seconds for connect operation

                        if (connectionFuture.isDone() && !connectionFuture.isCancelled()) {
                            logger.info("Connected to " + remoteAddr);

                            ByteBuffer buffer = ByteBuffer.allocate(1024); // assuming a maximum of 1024 bytes can be read from the socket for this example
                            channel.read(buffer).get();

                            MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");
                            byte[] hashBytes = md.digest(buffer.array());
                            String hashString = DatatypeConverter.printHexBinary(hashBytes);
                            logger.info("Remote address hash: " + hashString);

                            return hashString;
                        } else {
                            reconnectionAttempts++;
                            logger.warning("Connection to " + remoteAddr + " failed, attempt #" + reconnectionAttempts);
                        }
                    } catch (TimeoutException | InterruptedException e) {
                        reconnectionAttempts++;
                        logger.warning("Connect operation timed out to " + remoteAddr + ", attempt #" + reconnectionAttempts);

                        if (reconnectionAttempts >= MAX_RECONNECTION_ATTEMPTS) {
                            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to connect after " + MAX_RECONNECTION_ATTEMPTS + " attempts");
                        }
                    }
                } else {
                    reconnectionAttempts++;
                    logger.warning("Channel is not open, attempt #" + reconnectionAttempts);

                    if (reconnectionAttempts >= MAX_RECONNECTION_ATTEMPTS) {
                        throw new RuntimeException("Failed to connect after " + MAX_RECONNECTION_ATTEMPTS + " attempts");
                    }
                }
            } while(true);
        } catch (IOException | NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            logger.severe("Error: " + e.getMessage());
            throw new RuntimeException(e);
        } finally {
            if (channel != null && channel.isOpen()) {
                try {
                    channel.close();
                    logger.info("Channel closed");
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    logger.severe("Error closing channel: " + e.getMessage());
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses NIO2 Asynchronous Socket Channel for asynchronous network IO. It also implements a reconnection mechanism with automatic retry up to 3 times before failing the operation. The method is designed to handle exceptions properly and close the connection regardless of whether an exception was thrown or not.
']

