For handling external data sources for configuration updates, you would need to implement error-checking and possibly retry logic, or use asynchronous processing techniques like event loops or threading if possible. 

The time complexity of insertion is O(n) in worst case when array needs to be resized. Deletion is also O(n) because elements after the deleted one need to be shifted down. A hash table would have constant-time lookups but could have more memory overhead. Linked lists maintain order, which may not be necessary and could have higher space complexity. 

Peak traffic conditions can be estimated by simulating expected data input patterns and adjusting cache sizes accordingly. Memory usage should also be considered, as the cache size directly affects memory usage. Future maintenance and scalability should be addressed through modularity and clean code design principles. Avoid unnecessary dependencies between components to promote flexibility for future changes or updates.
