['The following is an example of how you might implement this task in C using a linked list data structure for each cell identifier (CI). It also uses pthread library to ensure thread safety by protecting the critical section with mutexes. The function handles delays or stale data gracefully, and cleans up any remaining memory on exit.

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

// Assuming LTE_RRC_CU_MESSAGE_T is defined elsewhere
typedef struct node {
    LTE_RRC_CU_MESSAGE_T *message;
    struct node *next;
} Node;

Node *head = NULL;
pthread_mutex_t lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

int insert(LTE_RRC_CU_MESSAGE_T *message) {
    if (message == NULL || message->CI == -1 || message->sequenceNumber == -1) {
        return 0; // Invalid input
    }

    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

    Node **indirect = &head;
    while (*indirect != NULL) {
        if ((*indirect)->message->CI == message->CI && (*indirect)->message->sequenceNumber == message->sequenceNumber) {
            pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
            return 0; // Duplicate combination of CI and sequence number
        }

        indirect = &(*indirect)->next;
    }

    Node *newNode = malloc(sizeof(Node));
    if (newNode == NULL) {
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
        return 0; // Memory allocation failed
    }

    newNode->message = message;
    newNode->next = NULL;
    *indirect = newNode;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);

    return 1; // Successfully inserted the message
}

void cleanup() {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

    while (head != NULL) {
        Node *next = head->next;
        free(head->message);
        free(head);
        head = next;
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}
``` 

This solution assumes that the messages received from external data source are fresh and not stale. If there might be delays or stale data, you would need to implement additional logic to handle those cases. Also, this solution does not include adding of new attributes for future modifications due to simplicity, but it can easily support additional message attributes by modifying the `LTE_RRC_CU_MESSAGE_T` struct accordingly. 

