['The requested task is quite complex, as it requires a good understanding of C programming, cryptography, operating systems, thread safety, and logging frameworks. Due to this complexity, I'll provide you with a simple example of how the library could be structured. The actual implementation would require much more code and thorough testing.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <dlfcn.h>

typedef struct crypto_algorithm {
    int id;
    void *(*function)(void*);
} CryptoAlgorithm;

CryptoAlgorithm available_algorithms[1024];
int algorithm_count = 0;

// Assuming that external libraries follow a naming convention like libcrypt_*.so
void enumerate_available_algorithms() {
    char *libraries[] = {"libcrypt_md5.so", "libcrypt_sha1.so"}; // etc...
    for (int i = 0; i < sizeof(libraries) / sizeof(char*); i++) {
        void *handle = dlopen(libraries[i], RTLD_LAZY);
        if (!handle) continue; // Library not available
        CryptoAlgorithm algo;
        algo.id = algorithm_count++;
        algo.function = dlsym(handle, "cryptographic_operation"); // assuming each library has a function named cryptographic_operation
        if (algo.function) {
            available_algorithms[algorithm_count] = algo;
        } else {
            dlclose(handle);
        }
    }
}

int main() {
    enumerate_available_algorithms();
    for (int i = 0; i < algorithm_count; i++) {
        printf("Algorithm ID: %d\n", available_algorithms[i].id);
        // Use function pointer, for example: available_algorithms[i].function(input);
    }
}
```
This code provides a basic structure for managing dynamically loaded cryptographic algorithms. Each algorithm is represented by a `CryptoAlgorithm` struct that includes an identifier and a function pointer to the operation associated with it. The `enumerate_available_algorithms` function searches for libraries named "libcrypt_*.so" (assuming each library implements one cryptographic algorithm), loads them dynamically, retrieves the `cryptographic_operation` function from each library, and adds it to the list of available algorithms.

